{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight","id":1457583,"title":"Silly thought about Twilight...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-24T10:59:41-07:00","id":1457583,"title":"Silly thought about Twilight...","content":"Yes, that Twilight. Sorry everyone.<br /> <br /> But it just came to me, and I need to run this by someone. What if the Vampires in Twilight actually are just a bunch of deranged, crazy Revenant families, who'd been abandoned a while ago and deluded themselves into thinking they're actually Vampires? And some Toreador is watching the whole drama for entertainment.<br /> <br /> EDIT: to clarify. I'm saying they are Revenants and NOT VAMPIRES. They believe themselves to be vampires, but they are not!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2337,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","user":"Quatar","date":". 08-24-2021, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T11:21:28-07:00","id":1457584,"title":"","content":"My thinking on Twilight is that it cannot co-exist with any version of the World of Darkness where both Mage and Vampire are in play or one day some ancient hoary Methuselah who\u2019s tired of his existence is going walk out to meet the sunlight and instead of meeting the oblivion they crave... they *SPARKLE*!!!<br /> <br /> I figure difficultly 11+ to resist the subsequent Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T13:14:53-07:00","id":1457591,"title":"","content":"They don't really work in the WOD without some massive houseruling.<br /> <br /> Obviously the sunlight weakness has to go, replaced with the sparkly in direct sunlight weakness.<br /> <br /> Generation and blood potency need to go.<br /> <br /> Humanity is still a thing, but it is cheap to raise, like 2 or 3 times level, and doesn't require ST permission, just a decision on the character's part to dedicate themself to a humane lifestyle.<br /> <br /> Each vampire gets one and only one Discipline, which they either pick at character creation or roll on a random table for.<br /> <br /> Strength, Dex, and Stamina are increased by 8.<br /> <br /> Perception roll difficulties are reduced by 2.<br /> <br /> For a while after first being turned, Strength is increased by 10, before fading to the standard +8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T13:22:01-07:00","id":1457592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457591#post1457591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't really work in the WOD without some massive houseruling.<br /> <br /> Obviously the sunlight weakness has to go, replaced with the sparkly in direct sunlight weakness.<br /> <br /> Generation and blood potency need to go.<br /> <br /> Humanity is still a thing, but it is cheap to raise, like 2 or 3 times level, and doesn't require ST permission, just a decision on the character's part to dedicate themself to a humane lifestyle.<br /> <br /> Each vampire gets one and only one Discipline, which they either pick at character creation or roll on a random table for.<br /> <br /> Strength, Dex, and Stamina are increased by 8.<br /> <br /> Perception roll difficulties are reduced by 2.<br /> <br /> For a while after first being turned, Strength is increased by 10, before fading to the standard +8.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So overall they are kind of like slightly better Thin-Bloods?<br /> <br /> <br /> All of that said, why are people trying so hard to make straight ports of Twipires to Masquerade when the OP's idea was that they are <b>not </b>real vampires, but simply a delusional ghoul family in a small town in the middle of nowhere? I'm kind of a little lost on that....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-24-2021, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T13:29:13-07:00","id":1457593,"title":"","content":"I mean, there is a reason I wrote that they would actually be Revenants and therefor not actual Vampires, they're just crazy and think they are.<br /> <br /> So why is everyone trying to argue with vampire weaknesses against it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T13:39:42-07:00","id":1457595,"title":"","content":"As others have mentioned, you can't really do Twilight in the World of Darkness as the underlying assumptions about vampires between the two media are incompatible.<br /> <br /> However, there's no problem being inspired about something and incorporating it into a VtM chronicle. Instead of trying to fit it in exactly, I think it's better to retain the essential elements of the story or idea and then reskin it appropriately for the WoD setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight#post1457583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Vampires in Twilight actually are just a bunch of deranged, crazy Revenant families, who'd been abandoned a while ago and deluded themselves into thinking they're actually Vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think this is an interesting idea and neat take on the basic story. Revenant family members have to encounter ordinary mortals all the time. I think either the Zantosa or Grimaldi would work best with that. Pick one or the other depending on whether you want the Revenants to act more inhuman or humane. <br /> <br /> However, instead of saying the Revenant family thinks they're vampires, I'd probably go with the idea that the high school Revenant decided it was just better to tell the girl he was a vampire and &quot;educate&quot; her so she understood what they were &quot;really&quot; like (like Revenants and not Kindred). Trying to exposition dump what a Revenant family is would just take too long and be less impressive. And then the rest of the family decided to stay with the story for convenience.<br /> <br /> The real issue is what do they intend to do with the girl? Is she new blood they intend to incorporate into the Revenant family? Is it some kind of sick game and they'll discard her when the time is right? It is a case of particularly humane Revenants and they are struggling on what to do with her? You could go lots of ways with it.<br /> <br /> I've only been able to make limited use of Revenants in my chronicles. And this idea presents some intriguing options.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T14:39:59-07:00","id":1457600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457592#post1457592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So overall they are kind of like slightly better Thin-Bloods?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Slightly&quot;? +8 to physicals is insane. Sparkling in direct sunlight is an insanely less punishing weakness than the thinblood weakness, especially since Twipires don't need any sleep whatsoever. They are much better than WOD vampires in almost every respect. The only sense in which they are inferior is that each one only has one Discipline-like power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T14:44:33-07:00","id":1457601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457600#post1457600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Slightly&quot;? +8 to physicals is insane. Sparkling in direct sunlight is an insanely less punishing weakness than the thinblood weakness, especially since Twipires don't need any sleep whatsoever. They are much better than WOD vampires in almost every respect. The only sense in which they are inferior is that each one only has one Discipline-like power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Misread that part, as all physicals - what would still be crazy for sure, but as a fixed benefit, something that blood buffing and disciplines can trump without too much difficulty depending on character experience. Anyway, my bad.<br /> <br /> Yeah, +8 in all physicals is OP as all hell, but that said i'm not sure the films or books validate quite <b>that </b>kind of physical boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T14:57:17-07:00","id":1457603,"title":"","content":"He casually stops a car from ramming someone, and doesn't even strain to do it. +8 to physicals is conservative.And he's not even supposed to be one of the stronger twipires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 08-24-2021, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T15:02:42-07:00","id":1457604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457593#post1457593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there is a reason I wrote that they would actually be Revenants and therefor not actual Vampires, they're just crazy and think they are.<br /> <br /> So why is everyone trying to argue with vampire weaknesses against it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Asked myself the same a few posts ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T15:51:25-07:00","id":1457607,"title":"","content":"I made a Cullen Bloodline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/936656-anne-rice-vampire-bloodline-a-bit-of-fun\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/936656-anne-rice-vampire-bloodline-a-bit-of-fun\"> Anne Rice vampire bloodline - a bit of fun - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/936656-anne-rice-vampire-bloodline-a-bit-of-fun\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/936656-anne-rice-vampire-bloodline-a-bit-of-fun </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I had a bit of fun making this and decided to spread the love a bit. Basically, this is a thread about putting various media vampires into the World of Darkness as </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It was part of a fun thread I did for adapting other media.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T16:11:54-07:00","id":1457611,"title":"","content":"I ran that the Toreador had sponsored a series of pulpy romance novels to romanitisize the vampiric condition to make kine easier to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T17:44:15-07:00","id":1457615,"title":"","content":"If I were to do something with the Cullens I would go the deluded thinbloods route myself who all have the daydrinker merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 08-24-2021, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T18:05:11-07:00","id":1457616,"title":"","content":"I love Twilight. These are all cool ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T19:00:48-07:00","id":1457619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight#post1457583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: to clarify. I'm saying they are Revenants and NOT VAMPIRES. They believe themselves to be vampires, but they are not!</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, despite not liking Twilight for other reasons, I find it extremely distasteful this macho insistence on trying to invalidate a story concept just because it is a romantic novel written by and for women. There is nothing particularly wrong with absolutely no aspect of its setting, or even with the quality of the write. It isn't good, but most WoD fiction is just as bad or worse.<br /> <br /> That said, engaging in the proposed exercise, it would depend a lot on what you want to transpose from Twilight to WoD. The basic premise of the story, or the same characters and feats?<br /> <br /> As stated before, Twipires do a lot of OP stuff. Their individuals powers are limited in scope, but would be at least Level 5 in potency right out of the bat, their physical attributes are so insane I would say they don't have +8 in every Physical, they have +3 and all three Physical Disciplines at 5, they never sleep or tire in any way, and so on and so forth. Most of the plot relies on their insane strength to some degree, so while it can be toned down it is still a case where they can't be too weak.<br /> <br /> With that said, I think we could do it. The Cullen could be a family of renegade Revenants, maybe with access to some ritual to turn mortal blood into vitae and other sorts of shenanigans to increase their powers compared to your typical Ghoul. They can and do accept other Revenants and Ghouls as refugees, maybe even Thin Bloods. I'd say a good starting point would be for the secret benefits of the family to be enough to roughly make them on par with regular 13th gen as PC starting characters.<br /> <br /> So, in V20 terms, a ritual to turn human or animal blood into equivalent to 6th to 4th gen Vitae, but the side effect of producing an even stronger addiction, maybe enough for a full blown Hunger Frenzy for human blood, and animal blood does little to placate the addiction itself. +1 dot to all the Physical Disciplines after induction, be it result of extreme training or the ritual-created Vitae. The Physical Disciplines and any one other (player's choice, but random from the character perspective) cost to raise as if the character was a vampire, but others can't be raised at all. Max Blood Pool doubled, so it starts at 4 and raises in half the usual time. Damage and healing is like an elder Ghoul already starting as if having 100 years, by page 42 of G&amp;R.<br /> <br /> If they think they are true vampires? Maybe. At this point what is the difference in definition? Where do you draw the line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T23:12:01-07:00","id":1457626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457611#post1457611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran that the Toreador had sponsored a series of pulpy romance novels to romanitisize the vampiric condition to make kine easier to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that is a distinct possibility in the World of Darkness. I haven't done anything about it in my vampire chronicles though.<br /> <br /> One of my Werewolf PCs considered the vampire romance genre to be an attempt by vampires to seduce more naive, willing victims to them and thus a tool of the Wyrm. He called it vampire propaganda. But the furthest I ever did anything about it in game was enter a bookstore and go on a rant destroying the shelves and throwing the books all over the place like a madman. I was forced to flee before the police arrived to arrest me. It was more of a personality quirk because there wasn't anything there for him to actually do as a plot in the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T08:17:37-07:00","id":1457638,"title":"","content":"As others have said, too strong for revenants. Also how crazy do you need to be to drink blood with a normal human digestive system? Blood doesn't go down easy and Diseases galore. <br /> <br /> You know if you just made it so that WoD vampires sparkled in sunlight and weren't weakened... well, the Hunters would be wrecked and vampires would be somewhat happier but most of the material would remain as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T09:00:47-07:00","id":1457639,"title":"","content":"Hmm... The sparkling could be a form of vicissitude or a vicissitude+fortitude combo. (Could be protean too, but that tends to be more animal.) Turn your skin and external tissue into a really thick protective layer that bounces the sunlight off and away from you but makes you look like you're glowing/sparkling? Vampires don't burn under thick enough cover, after all. Also doubles as armour, reflecting their &quot;rock-like&quot; flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-25-2021, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T15:26:39-07:00","id":1457652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457591#post1457591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Each vampire gets one and only one Discipline, which they either pick at character creation or roll on a random table for.<br /> <br /> Strength, Dex, and Stamina are increased by 8.<br /> <br /> Perception roll difficulties are reduced by 2.<br /> <br /> For a while after first being turned, Strength is increased by 10, before fading to the standard +8.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty obvious they have the physical disciplines and not just +8 to Strength dexterity and stamina. They are hard as stone and move at super speed while tossing trucks. They also can mesmerize people with pheromones and have a poison bite universally.<br /> <br /> Edit Eidetic Memory I think is another universal thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 08-25-2021, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T16:28:54-07:00","id":1457657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457638#post1457638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how crazy do you need to be to drink blood with a normal human digestive system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that's pretty common, <a href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/drinking-blood\" target=\"_blank\">at least common enough for there to be health guidelines for the practice</a>. A lot of people with porphyria do this to alleviate symptoms, although it is probably psychosomatic, and all around the world, including the US, a lot of people believe that ingesting blood cures certain diseases. Some also believe that it is healthy anyways (which it may be), and that is before talking about people that do so out of compulsion or lifestyle.<br /> <br /> By the way, human blood isn't worse than animal blood for your health. It is actually less likely to give you an infection or food poisoning, due to the likelihood of being heavily infected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457639#post1457639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... The sparkling could be a form of vicissitude or a vicissitude+fortitude combo. (Could be protean too, but that tends to be more animal.) Turn your skin and external tissue into a really thick protective layer that bounces the sunlight off and away from you but makes you look like you're glowing/sparkling? Vampires don't burn under thick enough cover, after all. Also doubles as armour, reflecting their &quot;rock-like&quot; flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are already 6+ levels of Fortitude that do similar enough stuff, so they could be a low gen family with heavy focus on Fortitude. But a combo with something else would certainly be interesting. Given Carlisle's command over the family, it wouldn't be completely out of question that no one among them is higher than 7th gen. Carlisle himself could be 5th, or even 4th gen. Or depending on how crazy you want this to be, he could be Saulot or a forgotten 3rd gen. Wild, but not outside the realm of possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T23:28:37-07:00","id":1457694,"title":"","content":"On one hand, there is a perverse sort of appeal to the Twilight Vampires being some kind of Revenant clan because there is something kinda... dysfunctional or creepy about Twilight vampires IMHO - something that wouldn't be immediately obvious in the sparkly surface but might exist 'deep beneath.'<br /> <br /> On the other hand I'm not sure they would really fit in with Revenants 'as is' in oWoD because Revenants were limited to one dot period. There were hints that might have been otherwise (and you can always replicate that through Ghoul's domitor generation or KoTE Dhampyr mechanics) but they still aren't *quite* vampires (KOTE Dhampyr would probably reflect this a bit better, though since they're genuinely meant to be 'half dead' rather than just a self-sustaining ghoul.)<br /> <br /> There's also some appeal to treating Twilight vampires as thin blooded (next closest to 'Revenants') - especially as you could argue the 'sparkly' effect is a byproduct of a chemical reaction (think small incendiary flashes instead of crystalline BS) - they're still burning, just much much slower.<br /> <br /> Mind you with V5 I think the differences between Thin Bloods and Revenant/Dhampir was blurred and they're all arguably 'Duskborn' so the difference could be said to be artificial. And given the kinds of merits Thin-bloods could take in V5 you could still give them more power than they might have with thin blood alchemy (discipline affinity comes to mind, although losing the benefits of Thin Blooded Alchemy and their usual means of gaining disciplines from blood.. they lose versatility for a limited set of powers) Might not be a perfect replication of Twilight vampires (at least and not be balanced) but it could be close.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another possibility instead of merits like discipline affinity. Trade TBA for the ability to use Blood Surge (possibly up to five dice). Maybe you can buy 'levels' in it (up to a point), or you balance it by paying health (superficial damage) to trigger it on a one dot per dice basis ('exceeding the limits' so to speak but also allowing it not to be so over-powered) First dot would always be free, and if you are allowed to buy levels you might even allow a second or third dot 'free' (TBA allowed for two 'dots' potentially)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 08-26-2021, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T04:06:47-07:00","id":1457699,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457694#post1457694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand, there is a perverse sort of appeal to the Twilight Vampires being some kind of Revenant clan because there is something kinda... dysfunctional or creepy about Twilight vampires IMHO - something that wouldn't be immediately obvious in the sparkly surface but might exist 'deep beneath.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they're vampires. Even if the author didn't worked that properly, it isn't hard to find them at least unsettling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457694#post1457694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand I'm not sure they would really fit in with Revenants 'as is' in oWoD because Revenants were limited to one dot period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know KotE's Dhampyr, but I don't see a half-dead state as that necessary. Twilight barely, if ever, touches the consequences of them being dead, nothing that couldn't be written off as just belief or lifestyle. Take food for example: they are all able to eat normally despite vomiting far later and Edward saying he doesn't like it. That could easily be an eating disorder accompanied by an &quot;I'm too cool for this mortal stuff&quot; attitude, especially considering that their attitude towards it isn't all that consistent and no real consequence is ever shown.<br /> <br /> The dots in disciplines are a little easier to solve, since they &quot;only&quot; need access to low gen blood. Be it through whatever means the ST deems fit, it isn't impossible to acquire, and once they learn the Discipline, as Revenants they wouldn't need more to just keep them<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457694#post1457694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also some appeal to treating Twilight vampires as thin blooded (next closest to 'Revenants') - especially as you could argue the 'sparkly' effect is a byproduct of a chemical reaction (think small incendiary flashes instead of crystalline BS) - they're still burning, just much much slower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Thin Blood would be a fair assumption, but then also a simple one to pull, if their lives focus entirely on the human side. But another option for V20 is the opposite direction, since there is no Minimum Blood Potence. They can all be low gen and yet young, and that would be enough for them to still feed on animals and have access to any means for reducing the effect of the sun as any 13th gen of the same age.<br /> <br /> Considering that Bardo is a thing, along with some ritual in at least two kinds of Vampiric Sorcery to do the same stuff, it really, really isn't that much of a stretch for the Twipires to have a ritual, Discipline or Combo that take care of the sun, the details are much more a question of theme than any difficulty for the setting to support it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T11:38:59-07:00","id":1457722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457694#post1457694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand I'm not sure they would really fit in with Revenants 'as is' in oWoD because Revenants were limited to one dot period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue about this. Revenants had Disciplines and could increase them normally. When they were introduced in ST's Guide to the Sabbat there is no such restriction mentioned. Indeed. we're explicitly told &quot;Additionally, vampiric Disciplines come easily to them. By puberty, most have <i>at least</i> three points worth of Disciplines.&quot; In Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand when talking about character creation rules for the True Black Hand's revenant families, they have templates for older Revenants where they are given more dots in starting Disciplines up to 10 plus more if they spent their Freebie points on it. And in the character stereotype sections, there are examples of Revenants who have 2 dots in a Discipline.<br /> <br /> As originally written, the Revenants can have more than one dot in a Discipline. It's not even clear if Revenants are limited to their Family Disciplines, or if they simply serve the same purpose as &quot;in clan disciplines.&quot; Although I believe I've only ever seen STs create Revenants who are limited to their Family Disciplines and that is what I do as well.<br /> <br /> It isn't until Ghouls: Fatal Addiction, a late 2nd edition book, where it's said that Revenants (since they are Ghouls) are limited to only one dot in a Discipline. I think that's more the fault of them trying to stick Revenant character creation into the same character creation as normal Ghouls. Much of the flavor text justification used in the section just doesn't make sense for Revenants. Unlike ghouls, Revenants don't have vampire masters who can provide them stronger blood. This would make Revenants <i>less</i> powerful than an ordinary ghoul with a 10th gen regnant. They don't have &quot;borrowed&quot; vitae - they produce their own vitae naturally. The rules also give Revenants one point of Potence for free which they did not have before. And if this is true, then why are the Bratovitch still given Potence as a Family Discipline? <br /> <br /> While the writers of GFA may have intentionally wanted to depower Revenants and make them more like Ghouls, the character creation rules are just a big mess that doesn't make sense and contradicts what was previously established. I would argue that that the character creation rules for Revenants in GFA are clearly wrong. They don't take into consideration that Revenants are different than Ghouls and contradict previous canon. It's clearly a mistake or possibly a retcon. I think it's more likely it was a mistake because the writer didn't want to have a separate character creation process for Revenants and therefore made a lot of arbitrary decisions to keep it in the same section. In doing so, he made a lot of errors that ignored what a Revenant was.<br /> <br /> I think it makes sense for ordinary Ghouls to be limited to one dot in a Discipline unless their master has higher generation. It doesn't make sense for Revenants for many reasons.<br /> <br /> Now as a matter of personal taste, if you prefer Revenants to be less powerful and wish to use the rules in GFA, that's fine. However, all the gamers I know have ignored the GFA creation process for Revenants. I'll be honest that none of us have ever played as Revenant PCs, but the few times an ST have use Revenant NPCs they were capable of using more than one dot in a Discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T13:51:13-07:00","id":1457731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457722#post1457722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's clearly a mistake or possibly a retcon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think it is a retcon, but a badly written one. The limitation on what a Revenant can achieve by themselves is clearly on purpose to me, and they keep the loophole where they can take on vampiric Vitae of low enough gen to advance more on a Discipline, but after that their own Vitae guarantees they don't need further blood to keep this power or use it.<br /> <br /> Old Revenants with access to greater power are easy to explain that way. For me it even serves a story purpose, as it gives then reason to trade service for blood with vampires. They have far higher independence than Ghouls, but still a reason to work with Kindred.<br /> <br /> But it is obvious that it was made without care, and easy to notice inconsistencies. It is not exclusive to Revenants, though, in general rules for mortals don't receive a lot of care and are exceedingly harsh in every possible way. Given that NPCs don't follow creation rules to begin with, those limitations from all sides are unnecessary and harm the game much more than they help.<br /> <br /> Personally I use to change the rules to make them more amenable on most aspects. Mortals are already limited by lack of several supernatural advantages. But when I'm not in the mood of simply changing them, I compensate with custom-made rituals. One thing in this case is that Revenants are old families, knowledgeable in the mystic arts, and they have one obvious advantage over vampires in researching their own condition, so it makes sense for those families, or at least some of their households, to have access to unique arcane knowledge and rituals that give some exclusive advantage or eliminates their limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T03:29:42-07:00","id":1457773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457583-silly-thought-about-twilight?p=1457626#post1457626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think that is a distinct possibility in the World of Darkness. I haven't done anything about it in my vampire chronicles though.<br /> <br /> One of my Werewolf PCs considered the vampire romance genre to be an attempt by vampires to seduce more naive, willing victims to them and thus a tool of the Wyrm. He called it vampire propaganda. But the furthest I ever did anything about it in game was enter a bookstore and go on a rant destroying the shelves and throwing the books all over the place like a madman. I was forced to flee before the police arrived to arrest me. It was more of a personality quirk because there wasn't anything there for him to actually do as a plot in the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> lol, I know the Order of Hermes and Verbrenna were delighted at the way Harry potter turned middle class British children into a giant recruiting ground.<br /> <br /> To quote mrs robin &quot;yeah kid I'm dimbly doo, now get in the van before the black hats arrive were gonna teach you how to use magic.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T06:46:57-07:00","id":1457782,"title":"","content":"I think it was the entire anglosphere, and even then I think I understate how big it was. I went from the UK to Australia for a school year and the first thing the kids wanted to know was if I personally knew/liked Harry Potter. Annoyed with the badgering of a large audience, I said I hated him (I didn't). The looks they gave me... I genuinely think I cut out a lot of potential friendships with that. <br /> <br /> Honestly tho, I imagine the Hermetics were annoyed the film was too Verbenna, and the Verbenna were annoyed it looked too hermetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T17:36:20-07:00","id":1457848,"title":"","content":"I like both Harry Potter and Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T20:57:21-07:00","id":1457860,"title":"","content":"Not only the Anglosphere, HP was quite a phenomenon and sparked a lot of curiosity about mysticism everywhere. You would find the same reaction here in Brazil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}